# Copy to .env and adjust as needed.

# Backend API base URL. Local dev usually points at your machine's LAN IP
# (see apps/seller-mobile/.env) so a phone on the same Wi-Fi can reach it.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.7:5001/api

# Google Maps integration point (src/config/maps.ts) -- the store-location
# picker on Business Details / Profile renders a plain address form (no map)
# until the relevant key below is set.
#
# TWO SEPARATE KEYS -- do NOT reuse apps/mobile's value for either slot below:
# an HTTP-referrer-restricted key (web) is refused on-device (no HTTP referrer
# exists there), and a package-restricted key (native) is scoped to one
# package name -- com.mechbazar.mobile is a different app from
# com.mechbazar.seller, so apps/mobile's native key would be refused here too.

# 1. Web only. Restrict to Maps JavaScript API + Places API, by HTTP referrer,
#    in Google Cloud Console.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# 2. Native only (Android/iOS, i.e. every EAS build). Restrict to Maps SDK for
#    Android + Maps SDK for iOS + Places API, by Android package name
#    (com.mechbazar.seller) + SHA-1 / iOS bundle ID.
#
#    NOT read from this file for EAS builds -- .env is gitignored and EAS
#    Build never sees it. Set it as an EAS environment variable instead:
#      eas env:create --scope project --name EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY_NATIVE \
#        --value "<key>" --environment development
#      (repeat --environment preview, --environment production)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY_NATIVE=
